---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import PageBanner from "../components/PageBanner.astro";
---

<Layout title="Welcome packs">
  <PageBanner slot="banner" title="Welcome packs">
    <span slot="box">
      Help us to welcome Refuweegees to Glasgow by taking over the welcome pack
      building!
    </span>
  </PageBanner>

  <div class="pt-6 lg:pt-12 flex flex-col gap-6">
    <!-- Intro -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-6">
      <div
        class="rounded-xl p-4 lg:p-8 border-2 border-weegee-teal lg:col-span-6 gap-2"
      >
        <h2
          class="text-2xl text-weegee-teal-dark font-bold border-b pb-2 mb-4 border-weegee-black/20"
        >
          Build your welcome pack
        </h2>

        <p class="mb-4">
          Welcome and essential pack items are always needed for providing the
          initial gesture of kindness that we wish to extend to all those
          arriving in Scotland.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          We've put together a wee essentials list to make building and donating
          both simple and impactful.
        </p>
        <p class="text-weegee-black mb-4">
          Details of where to drop off your donations can be found on our <a
            href="/your-donations"
            class="link">donations page</a
          >.
        </p>
        <p class="text-weegee-black mb-4">
          Please note that whilst the list below is our 'essentials list' we are
          happy to receive slight variations. We check each pack before it goes
          out so can add anything that's missing or remove anything bonkers!
        </p>
        <p>
          Contact <a href="mailto:enquiries@refuweegee.co.uk" class="link-teal"
            >enquiries@refuweegee.co.uk</a
          > with any questions.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div
        class="relative rounded-xl lg:col-span-6 border-2 border-weegee-teal overflow-hidden h-64 lg:h-0 lg:min-h-full"
      >
        <img
          src="/assets/welcome/welcome_totes.webp"
          alt="Welcome pack tote bags"
          class="w-full h-full object-cover"
        />
      </div>

      <!-- Essentials list -->
      <div
        class="hidden lg:block relative rounded-xl lg:col-span-4 border-2 border-weegee-teal overflow-hidden"
      >
        <img
          src="/assets/welcome/welcome_pack.webp"
          alt="Welcome pack tote bags"
          class="w-full h-full object-cover"
        />
      </div>

      <div
        class="lg:col-span-8 bg-weegee-white rounded-xl p-4 lg:p-8 border-2 border-weegee-teal gap-4"
      >
        <h2
          class="text-2xl text-weegee-teal-dark font-bold border-b pb-2 border-weegee-black/20 mb-4"
        >
          List of essentials
        </h2>
        <ul
          class="leading-relaxed font-medium text-weegee-black list-disc list-outside marker:text-weegee-teal ml-4"
        >
          <li>
            A bag, whether a gift bag or a rucksack – something to put all of
            the items into.
          </li>
          <li>
            Toiletries – shampoo, shower gel, soap, toothbrush and toothpaste,
            deodorant and sanitary or shaving items.
          </li>
          <li>Notepad and pen.</li>
          <li>Hat, gloves and scarf (2 of the 3 ideal).</li>
          <li>
            A wee token of Scotland or Glasgow – from tea towels to guide books,
            just think about what makes you think of home. Tunnocks? Irn Bru? Be
            creative!
          </li>
          <li>
            Something to read – varying reading abilities so all books
            acceptable. Please do consider the content though.
          </li>
          <li>
            Something to eat – this is very often also the token of Scotland!
            From highland toffees to porridge oats, it's always nice to include
            something to munch.
          </li>
          <li>
            Letter fae a local – your welcome letter to say hello, welcome and
            anything else you'd like to include. As long as it's kind then it's
            acceptable!
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div
        class="lg:hidden relative rounded-xl lg:col-span-4 border-2 border-weegee-teal overflow-hidden"
      >
        <img
          src="/assets/welcome/welcome_pack.webp"
          alt="Welcome pack tote bags"
          class="w-full h-full object-cover"
        />
      </div>

      <!-- Packs for children -->

      <div
        class="lg:col-span-8 bg-weegee-white rounded-xl p-4 lg:p-8 border-2 border-weegee-teal flex flex-col gap-4"
      >
        <h2
          class="text-2xl text-weegee-teal-dark font-bold border-b pb-2 border-weegee-black/20"
        >
          Welcome packs for children
        </h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed font-medium max-w-prose">
          We are also happy to receive welcome packs for children. These should
          follow the same essentials list above with age appropriate items and a
          small toy if appropriate.
        </p>
        <p class="leading-relaxed font-medium max-w-prose">
          Please ensure that the age of the child it is intended for is included
          on the outside of the pack. And please don't forget that we welcome
          teenagers as well as younger children.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div
        class="relative rounded-xl lg:col-span-4 border-2 border-weegee-teal overflow-hidden"
      >
        <img
          src="/assets/welcome/welcome_postcard.webp"
          alt="Welcome pack tote bags"
          class="w-full h-full object-cover"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
